2(1 + (k − 1) + . . . + (k − 1)(g−2)/ 2), g even.
Moore graphs are k-regular graphs with girth g that attain this bound. We
remark that all Moore graphs of even girth are edge-girth-regula r [14]. In the
case of edge-girth-regular graphs, Drglin, Filipovski, Jajcay and R aiman [8] gave
the following improved lower bound, which will turn out to be sharp for a number
of cases that we consider in the current paper.

