4 Improved lower and upper bounds for n(k, g, λ )
We implemented the algorithm from Section 3 (as well as the variants d iscussed
in Section 3.1). We executed these algorithms on a computer cluster for various
tuples ( v, k, g, λ ) to ﬁnd lower and upper bounds for n(k, g, λ ) (as well as the
corresponding graphs that attain the upper bounds). In total, t hese computa-
tions took around 6 CPU-years. If an algorithm was able to ﬁnd an egr(v, k, g, λ )
graph, then clearly n(k, g, λ ) ≤ v. On the other hand, if an algorithm terminated

